YANI (or is it YASI - yet another silly/stupid idea)?

The "mom" class.

Let me say up front, I know there's almost no chance this will ever be
implemented, and I know people look down upon new classes because the
current ones aren't even differentiated enough.  But I'm not posting this
expecting it to be implemented, I'm posting it because it's fun to think
about.

Secondly, I should mention this is not a knock on moms, it's a tribute.
If it sounds horribly sexist to you, it's likely you misunderstand it.
The fact that my wife generated at least half of the ideas for this class
should be telling.

Finally, I know some of the descriptions here are heavy stereotypes, and
some are probably America-centric.  But then, every class in Nethack is
one big stereotype; this one should be no different.

So, on to the description: the mom class.  I did my best to make it sort
of sensible, as well as unique.  Moms can be of any race, though I would
require human moms to be lawful.

Starting Inventory:

- +2 knife (the good kitchen knife, the one even dad isn't allowed to
touch)
- +0 alchemy smock (mom's apron)
- +0 leather gloves (mom always tells you not to forget your mittens)
- +0 dented pot (cooking utensil)
- food: some pancakes, bananas, oranges, carrots, slime molds, a bit of
garlic, a cream pie, and even a candy bar.  Oh, and some canned food (2
tins).  (Tweak this appropriately for difficulty...)
- 2 potions of fruit juice
- a gold ring (mom's wedding ring; subject to normal ring generation
rules.)
- uncursed sack (purse)
- a tinning kit (mom always comes prepared...)
- a tin opener (would mom bring canned food and forget the can opener?)
- small chance of: spell of healing or cure sickness (mom is good at
making you feel better) or towel or credit card or camera

Stats:

strength - 7-12 (sort of like wizards)
Dex - 10-15 (fairly high due to sewing, cooking, and generally taking care
of stuff)
Con - 7-12 (mom's not really tough...)
Int - 10-13 (mom's pretty smart, but she's no Wizard)
Wis - 13-18 (mom *always* gives good advice!)
Cha - 13-17 (mom is pretty.)

Gained intrinsics:

XL5 - warning (eyes in the back of her head).  XL10 - searching (she knows
where everything is, all the time).  XL12 - see invisible (cuz you can't
sneak anything past).

Weapon / spell skills:

Unskilled - most stuff.
Basic - short sword, mace, club, staff, unihorn (these are somewhat
arbitrary), darts, bow (from summer camp as a little girl), barehanded
combat, twoweapon (two knives prepare food *fast*), divination spells (can
always find stuff), enchantment spells (cause fear, with "the look"...)
Skilled - dagger, hammer (fixes stuff around the house), riding (summer
camp), healing spells (she's not quite a doctor, but close.  SPECIAL
SPELL: extra healing.)
Expert - knife.

Quest:

- guardian: Grandma.
- friendlies: sisters, maybe nephews and nieces, and possibly the old
family cat.
- nemesis: purse snatcher
- other baddies: punk teenagers, possibly leprechauns, etc.  Also rats and
spiders and ants and other insects -- the sort of things that crawl around
in the alleyways where purse snatchers might hang out.

Quest Artifact:

Grandma's lucky purse.  Unexplodeable bag of holding (it simply rejects
cancellation and other BoH's, or possibly makes them explode.)  Being an
intelligent BoH, of course, means it resists curses.
- carried: acts as luckstone (*lucky* purse).  Also gives 3 Cha if female,
lose 3 Cha if male (you should also get some funny messages at
Grandma's... "what the hell happened to you?" "is there something you've
been meaning to tell us?" etc.)
- invoked: creates a random tool excluding containers, magic lamps, and
pickaxes.  "You rummage around in grandma's lucky purse... you find a
stethoscope!"  That's the way it always felt to me... "mom, do you have a
bandaid?" "check my purse." "do you have aspirin?" "check my purse." "a
hammer?" "purse." "duct tape?" "purse." "fishing line?" "purse."
"third-grade report card?" "purse."
This does give a reasonable chance of getting a good number of magic
markers, depending on how many turns you have it for, but only if you are
diligent about invoking it consistantly.  Before you decide this is
overpowered, consider the orb of fate: half damage to everything.

Deities:

Lawful - June Cleaver
Neutral - Hillary Clinton
Chaotic - Martha Stewart

Special abilities:

Possibly has the same effect on eggs as males -- she is a mom, after all.
Possibly is able to prepare a corpse before eating it, adding some
nutrition and flavor, but taking some extra turns.

